		<h1>GridPermit Calculation Methodology</h1>
		<p>GridPermit utilizes regional US utility rate baselines, solar irradiance models, and time-of-use (TOU) battery dispatch assumptions to generate preliminary residential payback estimates.</p>
		
		<h2>1. System Sizing Baseline</h2>
		<p>Solar photovoltaic (PV) system sizing (kW) is calculated based on user-entered monthly electric spend divided by regional utility kWh pricing averages. We assume an average solar yield factor of 1,350 to 1,600 kWh per kW installed annually depending on regional solar irradiance.</p>

		<h2>2. Battery Storage Modeling</h2>
		<p>Battery sizing recommendations (13.5 kWh to 20 kWh) are estimated based on peak evening consumption offset capabilities. Under modern utility rate structures, battery storage captures excess daytime generation and discharges during peak evening rate windows.</p>

		<h2>3. Unsubsidized ROI & Rate Escalation</h2>
		<p>Payback calculations reflect baseline retail energy rates without assuming tax credit subsidies. Payback periods assume a conservative 3.5% annual utility rate escalation factor. Actual ROI varies based on roof orientation, shading, equipment selection, and utility interconnection approval.</p>
